# mpd.env — settings for this Moodle project.
#
# Edit this file to change how this one project runs: which database it
# uses, which PHP version, whether Behat is set up. Every setting is
# optional. Leave a line out and mpd uses a default.
#
# Two ways to change a setting:
#
#   mpd configure <project> MPD_DB=postgres:18
#       Checks the value, writes the line, and applies the change.
#
#   Edit this file by hand, then run: mpd configure <project>
#       Accepts any value. The second command is what applies it.
#
# To switch off something that is on by default, give it an empty value.
# MPD_DB="" means this project gets no database.
#
# mpd wrote this file when you ran `mpd create` and will never overwrite
# it. Git ignores it.
#
# Where defaults come from and which file wins when two disagree:
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, section 8.


# Database
#
# Which database engine and version to run, written like a container tag.
#
#   Engines:   postgres, mariadb, mysql
#   Versions:  a number (18, 17.2, 17-bookworm) or the word latest
#   Engine alone (postgres) means the latest version of it.
#
# Moodle needs a database. Without one, mpd cannot write config.php, and
# https://<project>.<zone>/ will not answer.
MPD_DB=postgres:latest


# PHP version
#
# One of: 8.1, 8.2, 8.3, 8.4, 8.5.
# Leave this out to use the default in
# /opt/mpd/assets/runtime/mpd-defaults.env.
#
# You can change it at any time. `mpd configure <project>` switches a
# running project over.
#MPD_PHP_VERSION=8.4


# Behat
#
# Set this to 1 to run Behat tests against this project. mpd then publishes
# https://behat.<project>.<zone>/, adds that name to the certificate, and
# points Behat at the seleniumv1 service.
#
# Off by default. Enabling it downloads the seleniumv1 image, which is over
# 2 GB, so switch it on when you are about to write or run Behat tests.
#
# To use Behat in every project, put MPD_MOODLE_BEHAT=1 in
# /var/lib/mpd/env/mpd-virt.env instead.
#MPD_MOODLE_BEHAT=1
